From: =?UTF-8?q?Moritz=20Mei=C3=9Felbach?= <moritz@glassine.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:38:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] ir3: no shifted SSBO offsets before a6xx (stgb/ldgb take
 bytes)

Since nir_lower_explicit_io can emit shifted offsets (max_offset_shift), the
SSBO intrinsics reaching ir3_nir_lower_io_offsets carry an offset in dwords
(offset_shift 2). On a6xx the lowered intrinsic only uses the dword source.
a4xx/a5xx also take a byte address: ir3_a4xx.c passes src[] "byte_offset" to
stgb, ldgb and the atomics, and with a shifted offset it holds dwords, so
every access goes to a quarter of its address.

On the Adreno 509 (Boox Note Air 1, Mesa 26.1.6) every compute SSBO store
lands in the wrong place: invocations 0-3 all hit dword 0. Keep byte offsets
on gen < 6, as before the option existed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (unreviewed; tested only on the A509)
---
 src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c
index 94810102c07..bc9c15d67b7 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler.c
@@ -452,7 +452,8 @@ ir3_compiler_create(struct fd_device *dev, const struct fd_dev_id *dev_id,
       BITFIELD_BIT(MESA_SHADER_TESS_CTRL) |
       BITFIELD_BIT(MESA_SHADER_TESS_EVAL);
    compiler->nir_options.support_indirect_outputs = (uint8_t)BITFIELD_MASK(MESA_SHADER_STAGES);
-   compiler->nir_options.max_offset_shift = ir3_nir_max_offset_shift;
+   if (compiler->gen >= 6)
+      compiler->nir_options.max_offset_shift = ir3_nir_max_offset_shift;
 
    if (!options->disable_cache)
       ir3_disk_cache_init(compiler);
